{
  "requirement": "`habeas info <selection>` MUST show the requirements and named examples matched by the {term}`requirements.references.definition_selection`. It MUST print matches in full-name order as Markdown with the same kind-labeled definition, Validation findings, Rationale, and Inputs structure and evidence states as mdBook detail pages, including readable output for missing or invalid evidence. It MUST work without a requirements index directive and report an invalid selection or no matches clearly. Habeas's bundled agent guidance MUST tell agents they can use this command to inspect a requirement or named example.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no gap against `requirements.cli.info`. Each obligation maps to marked code and, where one is needed, a test.\n\n**Obligations and code**\n- **Show matched requirements and named examples.**\n  - `src/commands.rs` `fn[info_markdown]` runs `inspect_repository`.\n  - It skips `DefinitionKind::Term`, so vocabulary definitions are never shown.\n  - It keeps the definitions where `definition_glob::matches(selector, name)` is true. An exact name matches only itself.\n  - `src/main.rs` `fn[main]` routes `Command::Info` to it, and carries `{impl}`.\n- **Print in full-name order as Markdown.** `inspection.definitions` is iterated in sorted order, and pages are joined with `\\n\\n---\\n\\n`.\n- **Same detail-page structure and evidence states.**\n  - `src/index.rs` `fn[render_cli_detail_page]` calls `render_detail_sections`, the code behind the mdBook detail pages.\n  - That function renders the kind-labeled definition (`## Requirement` or `## Example`), Validation findings, Rationale, and Inputs. It also renders the evidence badge from the state.\n  - `LoadedDetailEvidence::borrowed` supplies the evidence.\n- **Readable output for missing or invalid evidence.** `render_detail_sections` writes \"No rationale recorded.\" and \"No inputs recorded.\" when evidence is missing. It writes the findings block for errors. For an unparseable record it writes an \"Unreadable evidence record\" section.\n- **Works without a requirements index directive.** `info_markdown` never reads an index directive.\n- **Reports an invalid selection or no matches clearly.** `definition_glob::validate` rejects an empty selection or unsupported characters with `invalid definition glob ...`. When no page matches, `info_markdown` returns `no definitions match {selector:?}`.\n- **Bundled agent guidance tells agents they can use the command.** `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` (Workflow step 1) and `assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` (Workflow step 2) say to use `habeas info <selection>`. Both are attached to the requirement by `:impl:` anchors in `md/requirements/cli.md`.\n\n**Tests**\n- `tests/commands.rs` `info_renders_exact_and_glob_matches_as_markdown_without_an_index`:\n  - exact selection excludes `xready`;\n  - glob selection renders examples and requirements in sorted order, separated by `---`;\n  - the fixture has no index directive;\n  - the evidence badge, Requirement and Example headings, Rationale and Inputs sections are asserted;\n  - missing evidence shows Validation findings, \"No rationale recorded.\" and \"No inputs recorded.\";\n  - malformed evidence shows \"Unreadable evidence record\" with its JSON.\n- `commands_report_invalid_arguments_and_unmatched_selectors` asserts that `[` fails with `invalid definition glob`, that `nothing.*` fails with `no definitions match`, and that a missing or extra argument fails with usage.\n- `status_and_info_accept_a_definition_selection` tests the help text and an example selection.\n- `tests/outcomes.rs` `valid_fixme_remains_visible_in_status_info_and_book` tests FIXME state output.\n- `src/index.rs` `detail_pages_and_info_display_redacted_source` tests redaction through `info_markdown`.\n- Guidance text: the skill files are static markdown with no conditional or transformation, so a missing test for it is not a gap.\n\n**Unspecified behavior.** The `Sites` section appended for distributed requirements is covered by `requirements.references.site_review`, which `site_section` marks with `{impl}`. I found no other unspecified behavior.",
  "references": "a3d0c38492817c9bd1960df4661b18f916c694c63ee5950c30650d2a190366a2",
